      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You could start with a \"spectrum of change\" activity, using recent social issues they are familiar with. Have students research two different perspectives on that issue—one advocating for significant change (progressive/revolutionary) and one advocating for the status quo (conservative/traditional). Discuss the *methods* and *goals* of each group to illustrate how they approach societal transformation. This will help them see that \"progressive\" isn't just a label, but a dynamic approach to change.",
